                <pb facs="0681" n="583" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg583"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113 Arrow Air and Motors Corp./31:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-26T11:00:00+08:00">March 26, 1932—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 26—2:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>378. Legation’s 358, March 19, noon.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d643-f1"/> Following
                    from American Consul at Yunnanfu: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 25, 9 a.m. Legation’s March 2, 4 p.m., received by me <pb
                                facs="0682" n="584" xml:id="pg584"/> evening March 21st[?]. The
                            following telegram was received today from Waterman: ‘Governor General
                            telegraphs granting transit.’</p>
                        <p>The following telegram has been received today from Arrow sales manager,
                                Fisher, at
                            Haiphong: ‘Shipping planes tonight, arrive Sunday.’</p>
                        <p>Unless damage and unusual delays occur in transit planes should arrive at
                            Yunnanfu within fortnight. Notwithstanding Paris statement that an
                            absolute prohibition exists large consignments of arms and ammunition
                            have arrived here recently from Indo-China. Yunnan authorities greatly
                            appreciate assistance given by Legation and Waterman.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
